        "title": "Accounting - Field Map and Orientation",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Accounting is a **formal system for recording economic events and producing a periodic,\nauditable summary of them**. Strip away the vocabulary and it is a ledger with one\ninvariant — `Assets = Liabilities + Equity` — that must hold after *every* mutation. Every\nother rule (debits, accruals, the three statements, GAAP) is machinery for keeping that\ninvariant true while the underlying reality is messy, continuous, and contested."
